   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The weather and the seasons",
     "texto": [
      "To ask what the weather is like, say «Wat voor weer is het vandaag?». Common answers use the impersonal verb «het is», as in English «it's»: «Het is koud» (it's cold), «Het is warm» (it's warm). For natural phenomena, use «er is» or specific verbs: «Er is wind» (there is wind; in English we would say «it's windy»), «Er is regen» (there is rain; English: «it's raining»), «De zon schijnt» (the sun is shining). The four seasons are: «de lente» (spring), «de zomer» (summer), «de herfst» (autumn) and «de winter» (winter)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
